1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,769
Every December, hundreds of thousands of cars
drive home from Germany and Austria to Romania.

2
00:00:06,769 --> 00:00:11,187
And everyone asks the same thing: what do I need
to buy?

3
00:00:11,187 --> 00:00:17,973
The answer is spread over four toll operators,
four languages and a lot of outdated blog posts.

4
00:00:17,973 --> 00:00:22,844
And Romania rewrote its vignette on the first of
October.

5
00:00:24,465 --> 00:00:33,796
This is Drum Bun. Brașov to Munich on the
twentieth of December, back on the third of
January, in a Euro 5 diesel.

6
00:00:35,029 --> 00:00:41,281
The planner walks the route stored in Sanity:
every road section, the products that cover it,

7
00:00:41,281 --> 00:00:44,904
and the price valid on each day you drive.

8
00:00:45,945 --> 00:00:53,231
In Austria, two one-day vignettes beat a ten-day
one, because the drive home is two weeks later.

9
00:00:53,231 --> 00:00:58,054
The 2027 prices aren't published yet, and it
says so.

10
00:00:58,196 --> 00:01:05,323
In Romania the price now depends on the Euro
class. A Euro 5 diesel pays 26 lei a day.

11
00:01:05,323 --> 00:01:10,019
Without a known class, you pay the Euro 0 rate.

12
00:01:11,115 --> 00:01:17,803
Before you go: winter tyres in three countries,
and in Germany M plus S no longer counts.

13
00:01:17,803 --> 00:01:22,587
Munich needs a green sticker, and this car
qualifies.

14
00:01:23,645 --> 00:01:29,501
And the claims you probably read online, each
linked to the fact that corrects it.

15
00:01:31,510 --> 00:01:40,413
You can also ask the agent, in Romanian, German,
Hungarian or English. Here it checks two claims
from a blog.

16
00:01:40,851 --> 00:01:47,071
It reads the Knowledge Base through Sanity
Context, calls the planner when a trip is
involved,

17
00:01:47,071 --> 00:01:49,790
and shows every step it took.

18
00:01:49,902 --> 00:01:57,905
The Knowledge Base is built from official pages
in four languages, plus the blogs drivers
actually read.

19
00:01:59,284 --> 00:02:06,996
Underneath, every price is a document with the
dates it's valid, and in Romania the Euro class
it applies to.

20
00:02:06,996 --> 00:02:11,971
A keyword search can find it. Only structure can
choose it.

21
00:02:13,112 --> 00:02:16,513
When sources disagree, the build files an issue.

22
00:02:16,513 --> 00:02:23,407
I resolved them in code, and each decision
becomes a standing rule for the next build.

23
00:02:24,466 --> 00:02:32,320
It caught mistakes in my own data model. And
when a ministry page still quoted an old fine,
it flagged that too.

24
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:39,344
Against keyword search over the same content,
the agent gets fifteen of sixteen test questions
right.

25
00:02:39,344 --> 00:02:44,683
Search gets eleven. It finds the documents, but
it can't compute a trip.

26
00:02:44,683 --> 00:02:52,202
Drum Bun. Structured content in Sanity, so the
answer is computed, not guessed. Drum bun!
